BSD-2-Clause subcomponent: dav1d (AV1 decoder)

This package is an adapter for the WebAssembly build of dav1d, an open
AV1 decoder, distributed via the npm package dav1d.js
(https://github.com/Kagami/dav1d.js) and vendored for this project in
examples/basic/vendor/dav1d-esm.js + dav1d.wasm (sha256-pinned).

The dav1d decoder core is licensed under the BSD 2-Clause License
(https://code.videolan.org/videolan/dav1d). The wrapper code around the
wasm binary (dav1d.js / dav1d-esm.js) is licensed under CC0-1.0
(https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/). Both licenses are
permissive; neither imposes a source-offer or re-linkability obligation
on this package.

The Apache-2.0 license applies only to the glue code written by vigilkit;
it does not apply to the dav1d artifact itself.
